  "contributors": "Christopher Daniel Pang supplied the PAL/RPL/BLA and PECAN distinction between marker and payload and the two-view question. Hearthline derived the arithmetic tests, loss and funding bounds in his research program.",
  "formal_scope": "Small prime payload cost, uniqueness of a large prime owner, a fixed arithmetic condition using only factorials and gcd as the prime screen, unconditional overflow after removing five, and all positive upper-half boards. The universal gcd-only funding bounds remain premises of the RH conclusion.",
  "paper_scope": "The altered-frame loss for any fixed omitted prime q is asymptotic to n squared divided by q-1. Every row order and all prime-distance dials beyond ceil(3*n/bitlength(n)^3) fit at every positive size. Simultaneous funding for the intervening band remains open.",
