  "review": {
    "type": "author self-review",
    "head_and_boundary": "Positive n throughout. Endpoints p=n cost zero. The modified selector counts each newly admitted composite with radix m, not its least prime factor.",
    "asymptotics": "The groups q^j*p are disjoint; a summable uniform majorant in j permits taking the limit. Pure powers have subquadratic cost.",
    "funding": "The full-range calculation through one billion supplies the initial interval. The cutoff lemma applies to every integer above it. The frame is recalculated for each size.",
    "fixed_control": "Two concrete integer products are re-evaluated by the challenge solution. The RH implication has its own explicit quantified input; the counterexample uses a different selector."
  },
